# API Services

## Injectable

- Always decorate services with `@Injectable()`.

## Data access

- Inject repositories via `@InjectRepository`.
- Business logic lives in services, not controllers.

## tryGet / get pattern

- `tryGet*` returns `null` when not found.
- `get*` throws `NotFoundException` with a snake_case message.

```ts
tryGetUserById(id: string): Promise<User | null> {
  return this.userRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });
}

async getUserById(id: string): Promise<User> {
  const user = await this.tryGetUserById(id);
  if (!user) {
    throw new NotFoundException('user_not_found');
  }
  return user;
}
```

## Error messages

Use snake_case strings: `level_not_found`, `user_not_found`, `name_already_exists`.
